theorem steps_between_eq (start end_ : I32) :
    sb start end_ = ok (steps_between_val start end_) := by
  simp only [sb, I32.Insts.CoreIterRangeStep.steps_between, steps_between_val]

/--
**Spec theorem for `Step<i32>::steps_between` (general `start`, `end_`)**:

• Takes two `I32` values `start` and `end_`.
• Computes the number of steps between them.
• Returns a pair `(lo, hi)`:
    - When `start.val > end_.val` (empty range):
      `lo.val = 0` and `hi = some lo` (both components represent 0 steps).
    - When `start.val ≤ end_.val`:
      let `diff = (end_.val − start.val).toNat`;
      - If `diff ≤ Usize.max`:
        `lo.val = diff`, `hi = some n`, `n.val = diff` (exact step count in both components).
      - If `diff > Usize.max` (overflow):
        `lo.val = Usize.max`, `hi = none` (saturated lower bound, inexact).

